.TH CALDUN 1 "2026-06-20" "caldun 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
check\-temps \- report trustworthy machine temperatures and alert when hot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B check\-temps
.RI [ --notify ]
.RI [ --check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B check\-temps
auto-discovers the machine's reliable temperature sensors from
.BR sensors (1)
JSON output and reports them, flagging any that are running warm or critical.
Sensors are selected by a driver-class allowlist \(em CPU
.RB ( k10temp ", " coretemp ", " zenpower ", " acpitz ),
GPU
.RB ( amdgpu ", " radeon ", " i915 ", " nouveau )
and drives
.RB ( nvme ", " drivetemp ).
ISA Super-I/O chips (e.g.\&
.BR nct6798 )
are ignored by default because their channels are mislabeled on many boards and
report bogus values.
.PP
Thresholds are hybrid. When a sensor reports a hardware limit
.RI ( temp*_max " / " temp*_crit )
it is used; otherwise a per-category default applies. When both exist the lower
(more conservative) value wins, so a hardware limit can only make an alert fire
sooner. All thresholds and the sensor allow/ignore lists are configurable in
.IR /etc/caldun.conf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --notify
Send a desktop notification via
.BR notify-send (1)
when any sensor is WARN or CRITICAL.
.TP
.B --check
Self-test: list the discovered sensors and their effective WARN/CRITICAL
thresholds (and whether each came from hardware or a default), then exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All monitored sensors are within normal range.
.TP
.B 1
At least one sensor is at or above its WARN threshold.
.TP
.B 2
At least one sensor is at or above its CRITICAL threshold.
.TP
.B 3
A required command
.RB ( sensors " or " jq )
is not installed.
.TP
.B 4
No trustworthy sensors were found; run
.B sudo sensors-detect
or add sensors via
.B EXTRA_SENSORS
in the config file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/caldun.conf
Configuration (thresholds, margins, sensor allow/ignore lists).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1),
.BR sensors-detect (8),
.BR notify-send (1)
